==Strategy==
Due to its extremely strong and synergistic enemy composition, this stage is arguably the hardest revenge Advent stage in the game. Bringing a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] is strongly advised.

Use [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cats]] to shave off most of the first Gobble's HP as it approaches. They are the big backline baddies in this stage, and getting rid of all three effectively means beating the stage in most circumstances. Protect your Jelly Dumpling Cats from Pigeon de Sable using [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], else they'll get sniped just before reaching them. Once you're ready to engage with the frontlines, your priority should be killing the Zapies; [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]], [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cats]], and whatever other proficient nukers you own are your best tools to that end. You should always be looking out for the moment Wanwan finishes his attack cycle to get these units out up front. Note that Z-Killing the Zapies is high-priority.

Trying to fight the Zapies and Gobbles as a pair is a madman's endeavor, so save [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] for when the Gobbles come out. Timing him well can help instantly eviscerate them and thus reduce how much of a pain they would normally be to deal with. Without Defense Up [[Cat Combo]]s, Bahamut is unable to survive an attack cycle from Wanwan, so consider including one if you find it difficult to get value out of him. Your piercing attackers can finish the job if that burst of damage wasn't enough. It's highly likely you'll need to sacrifice some ground in order to get proper attacks on the many threats, but if it comes to the point where Wanwan starts directly attacking your base, don't panic. You should start thinking of its HP as another resource to utilize while you scramble to kill the remaining Zapies. Jelly Dumpling Cat's Wave Attacks will usually be able to push Wanwan back most of the time—things are not nearly as dire as they appear. Do your best to survive up until Bahamut recharges, since he can bail you out of a tricky situation by nuking what's left of the frontlines.

Once it's just the Zapies alongside Wanwan, things become a lot less hectic. They don't push nearly as hard without the Gobbles to assist them, although it's still possible to lose if you aren't careful. Nothing threatening spawns beyond that point regardless, so killing them gives you a clear sight of Wanwan.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] - Both of these meatshields are stellar for this stage due to their cheap costs and fast movement speeds.
*[[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] - Cat Chief is another choice for more anti-Zombie DPS.
*[[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] - While it is a limited unit, it could prove to be incredibly helpful when owned. It has strong anti-Zombie stats and has Toxic Immunity for the Gobbles.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Fishman Cat is a very useful choice for a rusher here, being a good source of disposable damage against the Zapies. His main selling point is that he does devastating damage against the Gobbles if he could connect against them, making him a very useful pick here.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Yet another disposable rusher for additional damage.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - If you find the Pigeons de Sable to be really annoying, Octopus Cat is an option to help escort Jelly Dumpling Cat and Cadaver BearCat.
*Talented [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - With a maxed out Slow Talent, Cyberpunk Cat could prove to be helpful in this stage, being good for controlling the Zapies and Gobbles.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Bliza (Uber Rare Cat)|Blizarena]] - A strong counter to this stage, being Resistant to both Alien and Zombie while also being warp and Toxic Immune.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] - Her Curse ability is very useful here, allowing her to shut down the Gobbles and even Wanwan if her Surge lands just right. She also has Warp Immunity, meaning that Wanwan can't just warp her away easily.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lone Moon Lunos]] - He targets every enemy on this stage, and with his Resistance, Toxic Immunity, Warp Immunity, Omni-Strike, Knockback, Strengthen, and Conjure, he makes this stage a joke.
*[[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Atlantis Logistix]] - Their extremely low cost and quick recharge time cause them to excel in a fast-paced stage like this. Their Insane Damage against Zombies allows them to severely cripple if not outright kill the Zapies and Coffin Zoges. Plus, they have a [[Cat Combo]] with Courier Cat that increases the [[Worker Cat]] starting level by 2, which helps a lot considering this stage is fairly cash tight. Their [[True Form]] only makes them better, as it allows them to stick around for just a little longer, to potentially land one more hit.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)| Supernova Cosmo]] - He can destroy the Gobbles in about 2 hits with his Omni + Wave, freezing them for a while as well. He can't outrange Wanwan, but he has enough range to reliably use the Coffin Doges and Zapies as stepping stones, and great survivability to tank a few hits. His Wave Attack can occasionally knock back Wanwan, doing considerable chip damage and giving very appreciated breathing room, letting your other attackers like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] to Z kill the weakened Zapies while Wanwan slowly walks back.
*[[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Wind Dancer Valkyrie]] - She is useful against the Zappies, having great damage and Z-killer. Her only problem is her survivability only having 2 knockbacks, but at very least she won't get warped by Wan Wan. She can be a decent choice if you can't deal with the zappies. She is also repleceable if she dies, having a cooldown of mere 51 seconds.

